  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3736",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with Kcna1 through a shared pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Guanidine binds to Kcna6, Kcnv2, or Kcna7, all of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is then linked to Kcna1, indicating a potential functional relationship where the binding of Guanidine to these potassium channel subunits may influence Kcna1's function. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent mechanism, with Guanidine potentially modulating the activity of delayed rectifier potassium channels, which in turn affects Kcna1. The overlapping roles of these channel subunits in the pathway imply that Guanidine may exert its effects through a common mechanism, possibly by altering channel function or expression. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Guanidine interacts with Kcna1 via a pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
